From 845e5cb6bd054b27a4a9671164ac86ab339d4e9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Ron D." <8740514+rgnv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:24:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 24/29] maps: fetch-on-demand + protected-map archives

The full game map catalog (melee, campaigns, scenario) plus community
custom maps live on the web host as a served mirror instead of the
preloaded MEMFS. When the engine opens a map that is missing locally (or
a zero-byte catalog placeholder), FS_EnsureRemoteMapFile pulls the served
copy through a synchronous fetch (per-segment URL encoding, catalog-
version cache-busting) and writes it into the emscripten FS; hooked at
FS_ReadLooseFile, FS_MmapFile and SFileOpenArchive. Non-map paths are
fetchable too (UI art, tilesets, long-tail assets).

mpq.c gains Storm-equivalent tolerance for protected map archives
(Spazzler/w3xmaster et al.): a 4096-byte signature search window,
malformed-header normalization (garbage sector shift), and archive-
relative table clamps. Verified byte-identical war3map.w3i extraction
against StormLib on a protected DotA map.

sv_lan.c announces sv_hostname (not the map path) as the lobby name so
the LAN browser shows a sane Game Creator.

Debug instrumentation (MAPINFO opens, fetch log, MPQDEBUG) is
env-gated/console-side; strip MAPINFO prints in a later cleanup.
